# UST.G3FI - H02 Component-20 Root-Ideal Normal-Pair Theorem

## Scope

This theorem upgrades the restricted conic identity in UST.G3FF to the full
ambient weighted polynomial ring. It does not yet promote the 100 finite
component-20 relations to characteristic zero and does not yet prove the
component rank is 36 over `Q(gamma)`.

## Selected root graph

Let

```text
q = xz-y^2,
r = w+G3(x,y,z).
```

The selected root graph is the weighted complete intersection

```text
Rminus = V(q,r).
```

The sequence `(q,r)` is regular: `q` is irreducible over `Q`, and `r` is
monic of degree one in `w` over `Q[x,y,z]/(q)`.

## Exact ambient identity

For the selected G3BI coefficient section, the six coefficient coordinates
of the corrected fiber difference satisfy

```text
A0_selected-A1 = r*B6 + q*D7
```

literally over `Z` in the frozen power basis of `Q(gamma)`, where

```text
B6 in Sym^6(x,y,z) tensor Q(gamma),
D7 in Sym^7(x,y,z) tensor Q(gamma).
```

The representative is canonical under the requirement that both quotients
are independent of `w`: `B6` is the coefficient of `w` in the ambient
difference, and `D7` is the quotient by `q` after substituting `w=-G3`.

Restricting to `r=0` recovers exactly the earlier G3FF identity

```text
(A0_selected-A1)|_(w=-G3) = q*D7.
```

Thus `q*D7` was the root-graph restriction, not the full ambient derivative
transgression.

## Normal filtration

The conic filtration in degree 15 has the exact dimension split

```text
dim Sym^15                  = 136,
dim q^4 Sym^7               = 36,
dim Sym^15 / q^4 Sym^7      = 100,
100 = 31+27+23+19.
```

The four summands are the dimensions of the conic quotients in degrees
`15,13,11,9`. This matches the four finite kernel layers observed at all 48
split fibers, but matching dimensions are not by themselves a promotion
theorem.

## What is newly closed

1. Both normal coefficients of the selected root complete intersection are
   explicit over `Q(gamma)`.
2. The full ambient difference replays exactly in all six field coordinates.
3. The restricted G3FF identity is reconciled with the ambient source.
4. The `100+36` count is identified with the four absorbable conic layers and
   the fourth normal carrier.

## Remaining wall

One must construct the selected Koszul contraction for `(q,r)`, iterate it
through the four conic layers, and replay 100 resulting relations against the
exact G3EX presentation. Only after that replay, together with an independent
nonzero 36 by 36 residual minor, may component 20 be promoted to rank 36 over
`Q(gamma)`.

